WEBVTT

00:00:04.980 --> 00:00:10.570
<b>Koudan Hospital</b>

00:00:06.860 --> 00:00:10.440
<i>Agenda 18
<b>\h\h\h\h\h\h\hAlignment</b></i>

00:00:08.440 --> 00:00:09.930
Tonegawa-san?

00:00:10.570 --> 00:00:13.320
Tonegawa Yukio-san?

00:00:13.960 --> 00:00:17.950
I'd recommend cutting back on 
fried food, sugar, alcohol,

00:00:17.950 --> 00:00:19.830
and cigarettes a bit.

00:00:21.200 --> 00:00:24.830
Oh, please. It can't be that bad.

00:00:24.830 --> 00:00:30.460
Well, actually... Just take a look at 
the results of your health check-up.

00:00:32.170 --> 00:00:34.180
<b>The Results</b>

00:00:32.780 --> 00:00:34.180
<i>The results!</i>

00:00:34.550 --> 00:00:39.180
<i>C! C! C! C!</i>

00:00:39.180 --> 00:00:41.790
<b>Needs Caution</b>

00:00:39.610 --> 00:00:42.270
The C that means "Needs Caution"!

00:00:42.270 --> 00:00:45.770
<i>C! C!</i>

00:00:47.250 --> 00:00:48.380
<b>Uric Acid Level</b>

00:00:47.530 --> 00:00:49.170
<i>Uric acid level: C!</i>

00:00:49.750 --> 00:00:50.880
<b>Blood sugar level</b>

00:00:49.750 --> 00:00:51.650
<i>Blood sugar level: C!</i>

00:00:52.210 --> 00:00:54.090
<b>Triglycerides</b>

00:00:52.210 --> 00:00:54.610
<i>And when it comes to triglycerides...</i>

00:00:54.610 --> 00:00:56.380
<i>D!</i>

00:00:56.380 --> 00:01:00.450
<i>Tonegawa is scheduled for a second check-up!</i>

00:00:57.950 --> 00:00:59.950
<b>Second Exam Scheduled</b>

00:01:00.450 --> 00:01:04.100
Th-This can't be happening to me!

00:01:05.850 --> 00:01:10.970
<i>Tonegawa Yukio, the number two 
man of the massive Teiai Group.</i>

00:01:12.250 --> 00:01:14.590
<i>He serves the monster 
of the financial sector.</i>

00:01:14.590 --> 00:01:18.970
<i>This shot-caller rose to the position 
of President Hyoudou's right hand man.</i>

00:01:20.470 --> 00:01:23.740
<i>This is the story of the battles 
he waged as a middle manager,</i>

00:01:23.740 --> 00:01:28.570
<i>in the shadows of the glory 
and fame he achieved...</i>

00:01:28.570 --> 00:01:35.560
<i>The small, unremarkable story... 
about the struggles of a remarkable man.</i>

00:01:39.570 --> 00:01:46.120
<b>Middle Management Blues</b>

00:01:39.570 --> 00:01:46.120
<b><i>Mr. Tonegawa</i></b>

00:03:07.950 --> 00:03:10.960
<b>Tonegawa Renewal</b>

00:03:08.180 --> 00:03:10.960
<i>It's a Tonegawa renewal!</i>

00:03:10.960 --> 00:03:13.580
Smoking increases your risk of pulmonary emphysema.

00:03:11.780 --> 00:03:13.880
<i>He switches from the 
cigarettes he was smoking</i>

00:03:14.980 --> 00:03:17.220
<i>to the electronic kind!</i>

00:03:18.890 --> 00:03:21.110
<i>His favorite yakiniku lunch</i>

00:03:22.220 --> 00:03:24.420
<i>gets swapped out to a lower sugar package!</i>

00:03:27.470 --> 00:03:29.730
<i>When the weather allows,</i>

00:03:30.140 --> 00:03:32.120
<i>he bicycles to work!</i>

00:03:38.370 --> 00:03:42.390
<i>He doesn't use the elevator, 
generally sticking to the stairs.</i>

00:03:45.640 --> 00:03:48.910
<i>He thoroughly modifies all 
aspects of his lifestyle.</i>

00:03:55.370 --> 00:03:56.920
Hey, guys...

00:03:57.530 --> 00:04:03.500
Why don't we try to avoid eating anything 
high in calories around Tonegawa-sensei?

00:04:03.500 --> 00:04:06.220
He's been working so hard to cut back.

00:04:06.220 --> 00:04:10.180
It'd probably bug him to see 
us enjoying that kind of thing.

00:04:10.180 --> 00:04:11.800
You're right.

00:04:11.800 --> 00:04:14.690
Now that you mention it, that's a good idea.

00:04:14.690 --> 00:04:15.940
No!

00:04:16.480 --> 00:04:18.820
<b>Psst... Psst...</b>

00:04:18.820 --> 00:04:22.700
If we really care about Tonegawa-sensei,

00:04:22.700 --> 00:04:24.570
that won't cut it!

00:04:24.570 --> 00:04:27.070
Huh? Doushita-san?

00:04:27.070 --> 00:04:33.830
Watching Tonegawa-sensei's efforts 
lately has gotten me really fired up!

00:04:33.830 --> 00:04:37.750
I'm thinking I wanna give 
him my full support,

00:04:37.750 --> 00:04:39.840
which is why I'm going all-in!

00:04:41.800 --> 00:04:44.440
I'm committing to Tonegawa-sensei's routine!

00:04:44.440 --> 00:04:46.410
The whole damn thing!

00:04:48.230 --> 00:04:49.390
Committing?

00:04:50.470 --> 00:04:53.390
<i>Tonegawa's discipline lights a fire in him!</i>

00:04:54.770 --> 00:04:59.650
<i>A fire in the heart of the former T-kyo 
Rugby Club captain, Doushita Kouji!</i>

00:04:54.770 --> 00:04:59.650
<b>A fire in the heart of</b>

00:04:56.980 --> 00:04:59.650
<b>the former T-Kyo Rugby Club captain!!</b>

00:05:02.870 --> 00:05:04.150
Good morning, sir!

00:05:04.150 --> 00:05:05.550
Doushita?!

00:05:05.550 --> 00:05:09.160
Feels good to commute by bike, doesn't it?

00:05:10.250 --> 00:05:12.520
I'll block the wind for you now!

00:05:12.520 --> 00:05:14.160
R-Right...

00:05:14.160 --> 00:05:17.670
<i>Tonegawa has no idea why he would bother.</i>

00:05:24.090 --> 00:05:25.300
<b>Psst...</b>

00:05:25.820 --> 00:05:26.410
Fight!

00:05:26.410 --> 00:05:28.050
<i>When he turns around, there's Doushita.</i>

00:05:28.050 --> 00:05:30.050
<b>Smoking Room</b>

00:05:32.310 --> 00:05:34.560
<b>Psst... Psst...</b>

00:05:35.320 --> 00:05:38.120
<i>When he turns around, there's Doushita.</i>

00:05:43.450 --> 00:05:46.110
<i>Every time he turns around, there's Doushita!</i>

00:05:46.110 --> 00:05:49.110
<i>What the hell is he doing?</i>

00:05:50.610 --> 00:05:55.270
<i>This might sound like making an excuse, 
but I've held the line well lately.</i>

00:05:55.270 --> 00:05:58.100
<i>So a little indulgence 
should be fine for today.</i>

00:05:57.930 --> 00:06:00.380
<b>Grilled ginger with mayonnaise and
pollack roe with seaweed lunchbox</b>

00:06:06.790 --> 00:06:10.600
<i>If I go cold turkey, I won't be 
able to hold out for too long.</i>

00:06:11.180 --> 00:06:13.680
<i>Time to enjoy myself...</i>

00:06:14.370 --> 00:06:16.680
<i>No! Cholesterol!</i>

00:06:18.890 --> 00:06:21.670
Doushita?! What are you—

00:06:22.280 --> 00:06:26.280
I... I don't want to have to do it, sir.

00:06:28.630 --> 00:06:31.370
But I don't want to see

00:06:31.370 --> 00:06:34.910
the sight of you losing to your weakness!

00:06:36.330 --> 00:06:40.830
I'll be as cold as ice if it's to 
help you, Tonegawa-sensei!

00:06:41.960 --> 00:06:43.340
<i>From that day forward...</i>

00:06:46.040 --> 00:06:50.090
<i>Doushita's involvement in 
Tonegawa's routine escalates.</i>

00:06:50.570 --> 00:06:52.340
Is this what he wanted?

00:06:52.730 --> 00:06:55.110
Here's what we'll do, Tonegawa-sensei!

00:06:55.110 --> 00:07:00.100
From now on, before you eat dinner, 
take a picture of it and send it to me!

00:07:02.860 --> 00:07:05.360
O-Only 36 points?!

00:07:02.860 --> 00:07:05.360
<b>36 Points.</b>

00:07:05.360 --> 00:07:07.390
<i>36 points!</i>

00:07:05.360 --> 00:07:08.780
Re: "Is this what you wanted?"

00:07:07.390 --> 00:07:10.330
<i>Roots and tubers are carb-heavy.</i>

00:07:08.070 --> 00:07:13.870
No Good. 36/100.
Roots and tubers are carb-heavy.
If you gobble down a bunch
because they're vegetables,
you'll pack on weight. -Doushita

00:07:10.330 --> 00:07:13.870
<i>If you gobble down a bunch because they're 
vegetables, you'll pack on weight.</i>

00:07:14.950 --> 00:07:17.370
<i>His diet is thoroughly monitored...</i>

00:07:22.760 --> 00:07:25.380
Come on! We're in the last stretch!

00:07:26.440 --> 00:07:30.630
One, two! One, two! One, two! One, two!

00:07:31.000 --> 00:07:33.860
Let's blast through the rest, sir!

00:07:34.900 --> 00:07:37.890
Think of how ripped you're gonna look!

00:07:38.370 --> 00:07:41.300
<i>His commitment overwhelmingly extends 
to Tonegawa's commute, as well!</i>

00:07:42.930 --> 00:07:45.900
<i>And after several days...</i>

00:08:19.030 --> 00:08:21.460
<i>Just to eat a fried pork cutlet lunch,</i>

00:08:21.460 --> 00:08:25.030
<i>I have to hide in the damn bathroom.</i>

00:08:25.030 --> 00:08:27.440
<i>What am I, some sort of bullied kid?</i>

00:08:27.910 --> 00:08:30.940
<i>But now I'll finally be able to—</i>

00:08:32.840 --> 00:08:34.450
I smell fried pork cutlets.

00:08:35.200 --> 00:08:37.450
<b>Psst... Psst... Psst...</b>

00:08:37.450 --> 00:08:40.450
<i>Th-That voice... Doushita!</i>

00:08:50.250 --> 00:08:54.470
<i>This is bad! I have to 
think of a way out of this!</i>

00:09:17.740 --> 00:09:25.690
<b>Psst... Psst... Psst...</b>

00:09:20.820 --> 00:09:24.890
<i>H-He's checking the stalls, one by one!</i>

00:09:27.370 --> 00:09:30.000
<i>I-I have to think of a way around this!</i>

00:09:32.750 --> 00:09:34.390
<i>He's here!</i>

00:09:34.390 --> 00:09:36.510
<i>Tonegawa is in trouble!</i>

00:09:36.510 --> 00:09:38.570
<i>Wh-What do I do?!</i>

00:09:40.310 --> 00:09:42.510
<i>Huh? No shadow...</i>

00:09:43.140 --> 00:09:44.550
<i>Did he leave?</i>

00:09:46.370 --> 00:09:49.520
<i>Tonegawa escapes by the skin of his teeth!</i>

00:09:52.870 --> 00:09:54.870
<b>Psst... Psst... Psst...</b>

00:09:56.110 --> 00:09:58.920
<i>When he looks up, there's Doushita!</i>

00:09:58.920 --> 00:10:01.620
Tonegawa-sensei...

00:10:01.980 --> 00:10:03.260
<i>Caught red-handed!</i>

00:10:03.260 --> 00:10:05.120
Th-This isn't what it...

00:10:06.600 --> 00:10:07.830
I told you, sir!

00:10:07.830 --> 00:10:10.130
Over and over! Give me that!

00:10:10.570 --> 00:10:13.350
Cholesterol is the root of all evil!

00:10:15.780 --> 00:10:19.130
If you must eat something fried, 
you take the breading off first!

00:10:20.340 --> 00:10:22.140
No white rice, either!

00:10:22.790 --> 00:10:25.390
Pork is good, though! Lots of vitamin B1!

00:10:23.740 --> 00:10:25.390
<b>Vitamin B1</b>

00:10:28.390 --> 00:10:32.900
<b>Koudan Hospital</b>

00:10:29.750 --> 00:10:31.170
<i>Several days later...</i>

00:10:32.150 --> 00:10:33.810
Tonegawa-san?

00:10:33.810 --> 00:10:35.750
Tonegawa Yukio-san?

00:10:35.750 --> 00:10:38.400
Please enter the exam room.

00:10:39.010 --> 00:10:43.160
<i>The results of Tonegawa's second exam are in.</i>

00:10:44.170 --> 00:10:49.670
<i>And for all his efforts, 
Tonegawa incredibly scores all...</i>

00:10:50.170 --> 00:10:52.450
<i>A's!</i>

00:10:57.620 --> 00:10:59.650
<i>A...</i>

00:11:00.680 --> 00:11:02.070
<i>A...</i>

00:11:04.210 --> 00:11:05.710
<i>A...</i>

00:11:05.710 --> 00:11:07.260
<i>A...</i>

00:11:07.260 --> 00:11:08.020
<i>A...</i>

00:11:09.130 --> 00:11:11.440
<i>A...</i>

00:11:12.950 --> 00:11:16.330
You did it, sir! All A's! A's!

00:11:16.330 --> 00:11:20.150
You're an A, Tonegawa-sensei! An A!

00:11:20.150 --> 00:11:21.150
<i>However!</i>

00:11:21.150 --> 00:11:24.340
<i>Tonegawa's estimation of Doushita?</i>

00:11:24.910 --> 00:11:26.720
<i>C!</i>

00:11:26.720 --> 00:11:29.910
<b>Needs caution!</b>

00:11:26.910 --> 00:11:28.880
<i>Needs caution!</i>

00:11:32.180 --> 00:11:34.120
Commit!

00:11:42.820 --> 00:11:45.910
<i>Another day, another release for Ootsuki.</i>

00:11:50.180 --> 00:11:56.180
<i>Huh... Someone other than myself is 
using the the one-day pass today.</i>

00:11:56.850 --> 00:11:59.890
<i>Don't recognize him, though.</i>

00:12:02.340 --> 00:12:05.950
<i>I see. He's got a totally harmless vibe...</i>

00:12:06.270 --> 00:12:09.100
<i>He never drank, smoked, or gambled,</i>

00:12:09.100 --> 00:12:12.460
<i>so his 500,000 Perica just 
gradually accumulated.</i>

00:12:12.870 --> 00:12:17.130
<i>He was glad to have it, but didn't 
really have a use in mind,</i>

00:12:17.130 --> 00:12:18.460
<i>so he spent it on the day pass.</i>

00:12:19.100 --> 00:12:22.770
<i>Sometimes you see guys like him, 
with all the presence of a houseplant.</i>

00:12:23.620 --> 00:12:26.970
<i>Well, as far as I'm concerned, his type...</i>

00:12:27.610 --> 00:12:30.970
<i>They don't buy at the underground market,</i>

00:12:33.350 --> 00:12:36.060
<i>and don't end up as suckers 
for games of chinchiro,</i>

00:12:36.850 --> 00:12:39.800
<i>so I'm not interested. Couldn't care less.</i>

00:12:44.050 --> 00:12:49.460
<i>Try and enjoy your one-day pass on whatever 
lukewarm nonsense you've got in mind.</i>

00:12:51.460 --> 00:12:54.290
<i>As for me, I'm headed here!</i>

00:12:56.580 --> 00:13:00.300
<i>A real hole-in-the-wall café that 
only true gourmets are aware of!</i>

00:13:00.970 --> 00:13:07.430
<i>You load up the apple pie with cinnamon, 
and wash it down with a royal milk tea!</i>

00:13:11.310 --> 00:13:13.400
<i>That's my...</i>

00:13:14.680 --> 00:13:16.310
<b>Psst... Psst...</b>

00:13:21.030 --> 00:13:22.920
<i>What is he doing here?!</i>

00:13:23.380 --> 00:13:27.200
<i>Or, I should ask, how does he know about it?!</i>

00:13:27.510 --> 00:13:30.790
<i>Is it that, since he doesn't drink or smoke,</i>

00:13:30.790 --> 00:13:32.890
<i>he gets his thrills eating?</i>

00:13:33.480 --> 00:13:34.960
<i>At least, compared to most.</i>

00:13:35.290 --> 00:13:36.710
Here you go.

00:13:36.710 --> 00:13:40.710
Your apple pie, heavy on the cinnamon, 
and your royal milk tea.

00:13:42.580 --> 00:13:45.990
<i>He ordered the same special as me?!</i>

00:13:49.850 --> 00:13:50.980
<i>It's him again!</i>

00:13:50.980 --> 00:13:53.500
<i>How?! Why is he here?!</i>

00:13:53.500 --> 00:13:54.710
Can I get your order?

00:13:54.710 --> 00:13:56.230
Er, uh...

00:13:56.560 --> 00:13:58.890
<i>No, no, I need to calm down!</i>

00:13:59.300 --> 00:14:04.530
Let me get a bowl of firm noodles with 
no oil, and extra veggies and garlic.

00:14:04.530 --> 00:14:05.850
Here you go.

00:14:05.850 --> 00:14:09.240
Firm noodles with no oil and 
extra veggies and garlic.

00:14:10.500 --> 00:14:11.450
Extra

00:14:13.260 --> 00:14:16.250
<i>The same order as me again!</i>

00:14:16.290 --> 00:14:18.250
<b>And afterward...</b>

00:14:16.580 --> 00:14:18.250
And afterward...

00:14:20.600 --> 00:14:22.300
<i>At every place he stops...</i>

00:14:22.300 --> 00:14:25.260
<i>Every single order is the same!</i>

00:14:25.260 --> 00:14:27.750
<i>The similarities stack up!</i>

00:14:32.130 --> 00:14:35.270
<i>There's no doubt about it... This man...</i>

00:14:35.960 --> 00:14:40.270
<i>He and I have the same 
taste! To a freakish degree!</i>

00:14:42.680 --> 00:14:47.160
<i>It's hard to tell from his expression, 
but I'm sure he's realized it by now.</i>

00:14:48.370 --> 00:14:50.570
<i>But neither one of them speaks.</i>

00:14:50.570 --> 00:14:53.970
<i>They don't share a single word. 
They don't need to.</i>

00:14:56.500 --> 00:15:00.790
<i>Because they're synchronized! 
A strange sense of unity is born!</i>

00:15:05.530 --> 00:15:08.800
<i>They end up visiting the same bathhouse,</i>

00:15:09.560 --> 00:15:13.210
<i>and sleeping at the same 
cheap business hotel.</i>

00:15:15.000 --> 00:15:16.810
<i>The next morning, at 8 AM...</i>

00:15:23.220 --> 00:15:28.610
<i>They continue traveling the same paths, 
never speaking, never making eye contact.</i>

00:15:30.730 --> 00:15:31.820
<i>And then...</i>

00:15:31.950 --> 00:15:35.830
Seafood
Bowls

00:15:31.950 --> 00:15:35.830
<b>Isono</b>

00:15:32.500 --> 00:15:35.250
<i>They end up stopping in front 
of the same restaurant!</i>

00:15:37.270 --> 00:15:38.780
<i>Yep, I knew it!</i>

00:15:38.780 --> 00:15:43.330
<i>Apple pie and ramen naturally leads to this!</i>

00:15:45.190 --> 00:15:46.840
Hey, welcome!

00:15:46.840 --> 00:15:50.340
<i>And of course, the order will be...</i>

00:15:50.340 --> 00:15:53.590
The minced tuna bowl, with extra green onions.

00:15:55.330 --> 00:15:57.970
<i>Yeah, that's it! The minced tuna here is...</i>

00:15:57.970 --> 00:16:02.100
Can I also get that with chili 
bean sauce and a quail egg?

00:16:05.170 --> 00:16:08.730
<i>Chili bean sauce and a quail egg?!</i>

00:16:10.180 --> 00:16:12.860
<i>I thought we had the same sense of taste!</i>

00:16:12.860 --> 00:16:17.120
<b>Chili Bean Sauce</b>

00:16:13.350 --> 00:16:16.550
<i>But he's going to use 
those things as toppings?!</i>

00:16:17.510 --> 00:16:20.620
<i>I would never eat it like that!</i>

00:16:20.620 --> 00:16:24.370
Here's your minced tuna 
bowl with extra green onion.

00:16:24.730 --> 00:16:28.350
And here's yours with chili 
bean sauce and quail egg.

00:16:28.350 --> 00:16:29.370
Thanks.

00:16:37.240 --> 00:16:40.470
<i>It's true that he and I have 
a similar sense of taste,</i>

00:16:40.470 --> 00:16:42.340
<i>but this is just...</i>

00:16:43.890 --> 00:16:50.900
<b>Munch... munch... munch...</b>

00:16:52.130 --> 00:16:54.400
<i>Is it good that way?! Seriously?!</i>

00:17:00.790 --> 00:17:02.910
<i>Should I ask for them, too?</i>

00:17:03.290 --> 00:17:05.150
<i>No! I can't!</i>

00:17:05.150 --> 00:17:07.420
<i>I mean, chili bean sauce is too much!</i>

00:17:07.730 --> 00:17:15.430
<b>Munch... munch... munch...</b>

00:17:15.810 --> 00:17:20.740
<i>But... it's not that I don't understand 
why he'd go for the quail egg.</i>

00:17:22.340 --> 00:17:25.440
<i>I mean, this is bound to 
go well with the rest.</i>

00:17:25.900 --> 00:17:28.210
L-Let me get a single quail egg.

00:17:28.210 --> 00:17:29.190
Coming up!

00:17:29.190 --> 00:17:31.060
Here's your egg.

00:17:35.330 --> 00:17:37.530
<i>As for toppings on a minced tuna bowl,</i>

00:17:37.530 --> 00:17:40.450
<i>that should be enough for me...</i>

00:17:49.090 --> 00:17:50.640
<i>This guy...</i>

00:17:51.370 --> 00:17:55.220
<i>He wants me to put my faith 
in him and take the plunge?!</i>

00:18:00.450 --> 00:18:01.700
<b>Anxiety</b>

00:18:01.050 --> 00:18:02.430
<b>Worry</b>

00:18:02.040 --> 00:18:06.700
<i>Ootsuki anxiously ponders for 
a moment, and then decides...</i>

00:18:02.100 --> 00:18:03.950
<b>Distress</b>

00:18:04.270 --> 00:18:05.910
<b>Anguish</b>

00:18:05.060 --> 00:18:06.700
<b>Pain</b>

00:18:05.640 --> 00:18:07.210
Agony

00:18:07.770 --> 00:18:08.730
<i>You only live once!</i>

00:18:09.230 --> 00:18:11.480
<i>He dives!</i>

00:18:15.430 --> 00:18:16.990
<i>Delicious!</i>

00:18:18.740 --> 00:18:21.360
<i>Unbelievable!</i>

00:18:21.360 --> 00:18:23.680
<i>The umami and spiciness 
of the chili bean sauce</i>

00:18:23.680 --> 00:18:28.370
<i>is mixing perfectly with the egg 
and tuna, intensifying the flavor!</i>

00:18:29.850 --> 00:18:31.030
<i>And the end result?</i>

00:18:31.650 --> 00:18:35.380
<i>A miracle culinary marriage!</i>

00:18:35.380 --> 00:18:39.880
<i>Ootsuki finishes his bowl totally satisfied!</i>

00:18:40.950 --> 00:18:44.670
I see... That really was 
an incredible combination.

00:18:44.670 --> 00:18:46.390
You're pretty good—

00:18:48.840 --> 00:18:49.570
Huh?

00:18:59.800 --> 00:19:01.750
Your time is up, too. Get in.

00:19:06.900 --> 00:19:11.330
<i>Ootsuki didn't see him again after that.</i>

00:19:18.150 --> 00:19:19.190
Foreman?

00:19:21.570 --> 00:19:22.710
Foreman?

00:19:25.240 --> 00:19:26.060
Foreman!

00:19:27.220 --> 00:19:36.070
<b>Daaaze...</b>

00:19:30.070 --> 00:19:31.250
Foreman.

00:19:33.620 --> 00:19:36.070
Foreman! Hey, Foreman!

00:19:36.470 --> 00:19:38.040
Foreman, heads up!

00:19:38.040 --> 00:19:40.820
Huh? Oh, Numakawa... what is it?

00:19:40.820 --> 00:19:44.860
Come on, give me a break! We need our orders!

00:19:44.860 --> 00:19:47.070
Oh, sorry about that.

00:19:47.070 --> 00:19:50.110
What the heck's gotten into you?

00:19:50.110 --> 00:19:52.950
You've been totally out of it lately.

00:19:52.950 --> 00:19:55.400
I know! Should we eat fancy tonight?

00:19:55.400 --> 00:19:57.520
Chow down on a T-bone!

00:19:57.520 --> 00:20:02.100
No... Sorry, but I'm not really in the mood.

00:20:02.100 --> 00:20:06.110
<i>I just can't see myself 
enjoying a T-bone steak today.</i>

00:20:06.110 --> 00:20:07.720
<i>I'd rather get the grilled mackerel meal...</i>

00:20:12.840 --> 00:20:18.980
<i>I bet that man whose name I 
never learned would understand.</i>

00:20:20.290 --> 00:20:24.240
<i>I wonder if I'll ever see him again 
in this vast underground...</i>

00:20:24.240 --> 00:20:29.240
<i>No. He might even be held in a 
different underground facility.</i>

00:20:33.700 --> 00:20:35.200
Something wrong?

00:20:35.200 --> 00:20:36.130
Oh, nothing...

00:20:44.580 --> 00:20:45.760
H-Hey, excuse me!

00:20:48.410 --> 00:20:51.890
Have we... er... met somewhere?

00:20:59.240 --> 00:21:01.230
Y-Your name...

00:21:02.950 --> 00:21:04.370
<i>Foreman Ootsuki.</i>

00:21:04.890 --> 00:21:08.490
<i>Even when in the clutches 
of the underground prison,</i>

00:21:08.490 --> 00:21:11.690
<i>he seeks to maximize the enjoyment 
of his one-day excursions.</i>

00:21:13.380 --> 00:21:17.880
<i>Where will his next one-day pass take him?</i>

00:22:55.450 --> 00:22:57.750
Next time, "Newcomers."

00:22:56.500 --> 00:23:00.250
<b>Newcomers</b>
